# Safety and tests

- `CLEANUP_SAFETY.md` is authoritative. Update it in the same PR when destructive behaviour
  changes; never remove, weaken or renumber a `SAF-NNN` rule.
- Never delete, skip, xfail or loosen a test; add or strengthen only.
- Never edit `tests/legacy/*.txt` or `tests/archtest/*.json`, never run the `update_*.py`
  scripts, and never hand-edit `tests/archtest/test_count_floor.txt` (`make raise-test-floor` only). A needed change to a locked test goes to the owner in the PR description.
- Tests are offline: mock `boto3`, Azure, GCP and OCI clients; no credentials.
- Assert fail-closed branches and destructive call order, not only happy paths.
- Use `parametrize`, `pytest.raises(..., match=...)`, `monkeypatch`, `tmp_path`, function-scoped
  fixtures; no `autouse` session fixtures.
